### Tested versions

- Reproducible in: 4.8.dev3, 4.7.1.stable, 4.7.stable, and 4.6.3.stable.

### System information

Godot v4.7.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1650 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9282) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-12450H (12 threads) - 7.67 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)

### Issue description

The "Fix Alpha Border" import option silently does nothing for image files that are in any format other than `RGBA8`. I would expect it to work on any image format with an alpha channel, such as `RGBAF`, `RGBAH`, `RGBA4444`, etc.

"Fix Alpha Border" import option in the Import tab:

<img width="369" height="487" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/59509650-90b5-4d57-bbf3-d0991156b2b3" />

`RGBA8` image (.exr files are not supported by GitHub, but the MRP contains the `RGBAF` version):

<img width="32" height="32" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/817c59b8-91ca-4585-9268-31a4918c4e20" />

Comparison table (`RGBAF` with the fix enabled is supposed to look exactly like `RGBA8` with the fix enabled):

<img width="800" height="800" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5bed2543-6b28-4097-a397-45b6fb13680b" />

The images in the table above were displayed with this shader:

```gdshader
shader_type canvas_item;

uniform sampler2D tex : filter_nearest;

void fragment() {
	COLOR.rgb = texture(tex, UV).rgb;
	COLOR.a = 1.0;
}
```

The issue arises from the [`Image::fix_alpha_edges()`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/io/image.cpp#L4297) function doing an early return (without a warning or error) for any image format other than `RGBA8`:

```cpp
// core/io/image.cpp

void Image::fix_alpha_edges() {
	if (data.is_empty()) {
		return;
	}

	if (format != FORMAT_RGBA8) {
		return;
	}

	//...
}
```

Note: The documentation for [`process/fix_alpha_border`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_resourceimportertexture.html#class-resourceimportertexture-property-process-fix-alpha-border) in [`ResourceImporterTexture`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_resourceimportertexture.html) does not mention this limitation. The documentation for [`fix_alpha_edges()`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_image.html#class-image-method-fix-alpha-edges) in [`Image`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_image.html) does not mention this limitation.

### Steps to reproduce

- Import any `RGBAF` format .exr file that has a transparent background (one is included in the MRP) with the "Fix Alpha Border" import option enabled (it is enabled by default).
- Verify that the fix has not been applied by either reading the pixel data via a script or using a shader to render the image without transparency.

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

[fix_alpha_edges_test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31078636/fix_alpha_edges_test.zip)
